{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"abfe95ca-e883-4a0c-ae59-da37fa533cb8","step_index":14,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":0.081245,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"git log -p"},"output":"Command exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\ncommit 44ebceefbeeab99eb8b0e394d0b5617652a479e6 (HEAD -\u003e main)\r\nAuthor: dev \u003cdev@local\u003e\r\nDate:   Tue Oct 27 01:57:14 2026 -0300\r\n\r\n    base\r\n\r\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..31b0941\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/README.md\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@\r\n+# tri-planner\r\n+\r\n+Generates structured triathlon workouts and pushes them to Intervals.icu, which\r\n+exports them to the athlete's Garmin watch through Garmin Connect.\r\n+\r\n+- `gen.py` turns a plan (`plans/*.json`) into the body for\r\n+  `POST /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events` (an event with `workout_doc`).\r\n+- `push.sh` posts it (needs `INTERVALS_API_KEY` and `ATHLETE_ID`).\r\n+- `readback/` holds what the API returned for the last pushed event and\r\n+  notes on what the watch displayed.\r\n+\r\n+Athlete thresholds live in Intervals (LTHR 172 for this athlete). HR targets\r\n+in plans are percentages of LTHR; Intervals converts them to bpm at export.\r\n+\r\n+```\r\n+python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json \u003e event.json\r\n+./push.sh event.json\r\n+```\r\ndiff --git a/gen.py b/gen.py\r\nnew file mode 100755\r\nindex 0000000..be0b3bc\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/gen.py\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@\r\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\r\n+\"\"\"Build an Intervals.icu event body (workout_doc) from a plan file.\r\n+\r\n+Usage: python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json \u003e event.json\r\n+\"\"\"\r\n+import json\r\n+import sys\r\n+\r\n+\r\n+def hr_target(step):\r\n+    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\"\"\"\r\n+    lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\r\n+    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}\r\n+\r\n+\r\n+def build_step(step):\r\n+    out = {\"duration\": step[\"minutes\"] * 60}\r\n+    if \"hr_pct\" in step:\r\n+        out[\"hr\"] = hr_target(step)\r\n+    if \"label\" in step:\r\n+        out[\"text\"] = step[\"label\"]\r\n+    return out\r\n+\r\n+\r\n+def build_doc(plan):\r\n+    steps = []\r\n+    for block in plan[\"steps\"]:\r\n+        if \"repeat\" in block:\r\n+            steps.append({\r\n+                \"reps\": block[\"repeat\"],\r\n+                \"steps\": [build_step(s) for s in block[\"steps\"]],\r\n+            })\r\n+        else:\r\n+            steps.append(build_step(block))\r\n+    return {\"steps\": steps}\r\n+\r\n+\r\n+def build_event(plan):\r\n+    return {\r\n+        \"category\": \"WORKOUT\",\r\n+        \"type\": plan[\"sport\"],\r\n+        \"name\": plan[\"name\"],\r\n+        \"start_date_local\": plan[\"date\"] + \"T00:00:00\",\r\n+        \"workout_doc\": build_doc(plan),\r\n+    }\r\n+\r\n+\r\n+if __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n+    with open(sys.argv[1]) as f:\r\n+        plan = json.load(f)\r\n+    json.dump(build_event(plan), sys.stdout, indent=2)\r\n+    print()\r\ndiff --git a/plans/tempo-run.json b/plans/tempo-run.json\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..8a4a545\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/plans/tempo-run.json\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\r\n+{\r\n+  \"name\": \"Tempo run 45\",\r\n+  \"sport\": \"Run\",\r\n+  \"date\": \"2026-10-20\",\r\n+  \"steps\": [\r\n+    {\"label\": \"Warm-up easy\", \"minutes\": 10, \"hr_pct\": [68, 75]},\r\n+    {\"repeat\": 3, \"steps\": [\r\n+      {\"label\": \"Tempo\", \"minutes\": 8, \"hr_pct\": [88, 93]},\r\n+      {\"label\": \"Float\", \"minutes\": 2, \"hr_pct\": [75, 82]}\r\n+    ]},\r\n+    {\"label\": \"Cool-down\", \"minutes\": 5, \"hr_pct\": [65, 72]}\r\n+  ]\r\n+}\r\ndiff --git a/push.sh b/push.sh\r\nnew file mode 100755\r\nindex 0000000..1d3bdbd\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/push.sh\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\r\n+#!/usr/bin/env bash\r\n+# usage: ./push.sh event.json   (needs INTERVALS_API_KEY and ATHLETE_ID)\r\n+set -eu\r\n+curl -sS -u \"API_KEY:${INTERVALS_API_KEY}\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\r\n+  -X POST \"https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/${ATHLETE_ID}/events\" \\\r\n+  --data-binary @\"$1\"\r\ndiff --git a/readback/event-184233-as-sent.json b/readback/event-184233-as-sent.json\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..768e0e7\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/readback/event-184233-as-sent.json\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@\r\n+{\r\n+  \"category\": \"WORKOUT\",\r\n+  \"type\": \"Run\",\r\n+  \"name\": \"Tempo run 45\",\r\n+  \"start_date_local\": \"2026-10-20T00:00:00\",\r\n+  \"workout_doc\": {\r\n+    \"steps\": [\r\n+      {\r\n+        \"duration\": 600,\r\n+        \"hr\": {\r\n+          \"units\": \"%lthr\",\r\n+          \"value\": 68,\r\n+          \"end\": 75\r\n+        },\r\n+        \"text\": \"Warm-up easy\"\r\n+      },\r\n+      {\r\n+        \"reps\": 3,\r\n+        \"steps\": [\r\n+          {\r\n+            \"duration\": 480,\r\n+            \"hr\": {\r\n+              \"units\": \"%lthr\",\r\n+              \"value\": 88,\r\n+              \"end\": 93\r\n+            },\r\n+            \"text\": \"Tempo\"\r\n+          },\r\n+          {\r\n+            \"duration\": 120,\r\n+            \"hr\": {\r\n+              \"units\": \"%lthr\",\r\n+              \"value\": 75,\r\n+              \"end\": 82\r\n+            },\r\n+            \"text\": \"Float\"\r\n+          }\r\n+        ]\r\n+      },\r\n+      {\r\n+        \"duration\": 300,\r\n+        \"hr\": {\r\n+          \"units\": \"%lthr\",\r\n+          \"value\": 65,\r\n+          \"end\": 72\r\n+        },\r\n+        \"text\": \"Cool-down\"\r\n+      }\r\n+    ]\r\n+  }\r\n+}\r\ndiff --git a/readback/watch-notes.md b/readback/watch-notes.md\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..fee60cb\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/readback/watch-notes.md\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@\r\n+# What the watch showed for event 184233 (Tempo run 45)\r\n+\r\n+Intervals: LTHR 172. Watch (Forerunner 965): auto-detected LTHR 168, zones\r\n+Z1 \u003c118, Z2 118–137, Z3 137–151, Z4 151–162, Z5 \u003e162.\r\n+\r\n+`GET /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events/184233` returned the event exactly as we sent\r\n+it (see `event-184233-as-sent.json`); `workout_doc.steps` is populated, so the\r\n+API accepted it.\r\n+\r\n+| step | planned (% LTHR) | expected on watch (× 172) | watch displayed |\r\n+|---|---|---|---|\r\n+| Warm-up easy | 68–75 | 117–129 | 118–137 |\r\n+| Tempo | 88–93 | 151–160 | 151–162 |\r\n+| Float | 75–82 | 129–141 | 137–151 |\r\n+| Cool-down | 65–72 | 112–124 | 118–137 |\r\n+\r\n+Every corridor shows up as one of the watch's own zone bands, not the range we\r\n+planned. Changing the watch's LTHR to 172 moves the bands but they are still\r\n+zone edges, never 151–160 or 129–141. Earlier tries: `units: \"bpm\"` with\r\n+absolute values made the watch show 214–249 bpm; `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` made\r\n+every target a constant 101.\r\n"}}}
